Feature: Automate migration of files from Purgo S3 landing folder to archive folder

  Background:
    Given the Databricks secret scope "aws_keys" is set up with access_key and secret_key
    And the Unity Catalog is set to "purgo_databricks" and schema is set to "purgo_playground"

  Scenario Outline: Successful file migration
    Given the s3_file_process_log table has the following records:
      | file_name | s3_landing_path                              | s3_archive_path                              | file_status |
      | <file_name> | <s3_landing_path> | <s3_archive_path> | SUCCESS    |
    When the PySpark script is executed
    Then the file is moved from s3_landing_path to s3_archive_path
    And the wrk_s3_file_migration_audit table has a new record with:
      | file_name | action | source_path | target_path | status | reason | timestamp |
      | <file_name> | MOVE   | <s3_landing_path> | <s3_archive_path> | SUCCESS |  | <current_timestamp> |

    Examples:
      | file_name | s3_landing_path                              | s3_archive_path                              |
      | file1.txt | s3://agilisium-playground-dev/filestore/purgo/patient_raw | s3://agilisium-playground-dev/filestore/purgo/patient_raw_archive |
      | file2.txt | s3://agilisium-playground-dev/filestore/purgo/patient_raw | s3://agilisium-playground-dev/filestore/purgo/patient_raw_archive |

  Scenario Outline: File not found in s3_landing_path
    Given the s3_file_process_log table has the following records:
      | file_name | s3_landing_path                              | s3_archive_path                              | file_status |
      | <file_name> | <s3_landing_path> | <s3_archive_path> | SUCCESS    |
    And the file does not exist in s3_landing_path
    When the PySpark script is executed
    Then the file is not moved
    And the wrk_s3_file_migration_audit table has a new record with:
      | file_name | action | source_path | target_path | status | reason | timestamp |
      | <file_name> | MOVE   | <s3_landing_path> | <s3_archive_path> | FAILED | File not found | <current_timestamp> |

    Examples:
      | file_name | s3_landing_path                              | s3_archive_path                              |
      | file1.txt | s3://agilisium-playground-dev/filestore/purgo/patient_raw | s3://agilisium-playground-dev/filestore/purgo/patient_raw_archive |
      | file2.txt | s3://agilisium-playground-dev/filestore/purgo/patient_raw | s3://agilisium-playground-dev/filestore/purgo/patient_raw_archive |

  Scenario Outline: Invalid s3_archive_path
    Given the s3_file_process_log table has the following records:
      | file_name | s3_landing_path                              | s3_archive_path                              | file_status |
      | <file_name> | <s3_landing_path> | <s3_archive_path> | SUCCESS    |
    And the s3_archive_path is invalid
    When the PySpark script is executed
    Then the file is not moved
    And the wrk_s3_file_migration_audit table has a new record with:
      | file_name | action | source_path | target_path | status | reason | timestamp |
      | <file_name> | MOVE   | <s3_landing_path> | <s3_archive_path> | FAILED | Invalid archive path | <current_timestamp> |

    Examples:
      | file_name | s3_landing_path                              | s3_archive_path                              |
      | file1.txt | s3://agilisium-playground-dev/filestore/purgo/patient_raw | s3://invalid-archive-path |
      | file2.txt | s3://agilisium-playground-dev/filestore/purgo/patient_raw | s3://invalid-archive-path |

  Scenario Outline: File status is not SUCCESS
    Given the s3_file_process_log table has the following records:
      | file_name | s3_landing_path                              | s3_archive_path                              | file_status |
      | <file_name> | <s3_landing_path> | <s3_archive_path> | <file_status> |
    When the PySpark script is executed
    Then the file is not moved
    And the wrk_s3_file_migration_audit table does not have a new record

    Examples:
      | file_name | s3_landing_path                              | s3_archive_path                              | file_status |
      | file1.txt | s3://agilisium-playground-dev/filestore/purgo/patient_raw | s3://agilisium-playground-dev/filestore/purgo/patient_raw_archive | FAILED    |
      | file2.txt | s3://agilisium-playground-dev/filestore/purgo/patient_raw | s3://agilisium-playground-dev/filestore/purgo/patient_raw_archive | PENDING   |
